Anyone who has got the latest release will, I am sure, have read the
modguide.tex document by now; this describes our policy on
distributing and modifying files from the LaTeX distribution.
 
A copy of this was sent to Richard Stallman of the Free Software
Foundation, since he was one of the people who asked us to clarify our
conditions.
 
I shall soon be psoting here some of his comments, questions and
statements because we believe that this debate should involve users
and LaTeX system support people: what kind of a system do you want?
 
Is a document file the same as a file of code?
 
 
